// Category: SAPIC translation corners of `let`, with the
// translation-progress option (sapic_lets_plain is the twin).
//
//   - a destructor `let` whose else-branch fails: only the rules that
//     merely match an equation skip the derivation checks (the wf block runs
//     them; sapic_lets_reliable_* repeat this over a reliable channel);
//   - a nullary destructor whose equation and failure premises coincide:
//     both rules share the derivation attributes;
//   - a pattern `let` with the else branch omitted keeps its failure
//     restriction;
//   - an embedded MSR step's `_restrict` survives rule compression.
// No corpus theory has translation-progress with an embedded restriction,
// and the corpus derivation-check regression covers the plain wrapper only.

theory SapicLets_progress
begin

options: translation-progress

functions: d/1 [destructor], wrap/1, d0/0 [destructor], ok/0

equations: d(wrap(x)) = x

process:
  ( in(x); let y = d(d(x)) in out(y) else event Failed() )
  || ( let y0 = d0() in event Seen(y0) else event Wrong() )
  || ( in(x2); let <a, b> = x2 in event A(a, b) )
  || ( [ ] --[ _restrict(F) ]-> [ ]; event E() )

end
